  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1236 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nHot and dry weather will persist across the area through much of \nthe long term period. The upper level ridge will reposition itself \nacross the southeast CONUS through mid week. West Central Texas \nwill remain on the western periphery of the upper ridge, which will \nresult in slightly cooler temperatures compared to our current \ntemperatures. Highs through mid week will be in the upper 90s to \naround 102 degrees. Still looks like a pattern change as we head \ntowards next weekend, as models show a shortwave moving across the\nCentral Plains. This would support cooler temperatures and some \nrain chances across the area. Temperatures are expected to cool \nto near normal by the weekend, with low rain chances (20 to 30%) \nreturning.",
